- [x] "Back up the database" was a DATA-LOSS instruction and nothing said so. The hub
      opens SQLite with journal_mode(WAL), so a live hub can have a 4096-BYTE
      lintel.db beside a 1.8 MiB lintel.db-wal — measured, and now pinned by a test.
      Copying the .db alone gives a file that opens, reports ZERO integrity faults,
      and does not contain the tables, because an empty database is a valid one. The
      integrity check added yesterday cannot see this: the copy is not damaged, it is
      empty. After a checkpoint it is worse, because the copy looks complete and is
      merely missing everything since. A whole-directory copy replays correctly under
      OpenReadOnly (50/50 rows), so the fix is instructions plus visibility.
      verify-restore now reports the WAL's size when present, and when ABSENT says it
      cannot tell a clean checkpoint from a copy that omitted the file — they are
      identical on disk. hub/README says all of it.
