      hub start and then answer wrongly) on the read-only handle it already had.
      MY OWN NEW CODE had an untested branch and a tamper found it: both damage
      shapes make SQLite abandon the pragma and ERROR, so the fault-ROW collecting
      path ran in nothing, and dropping every collected fault was NOT CAUGHT. Getting
      rows needs damage to a page HEADER (b-tree page header -> "btreeInitPage()
      returns error code 11" as a row); damage to cell content at the page END is
      fatal at open instead, which is why my first fixture found nothing. Both
      tampers caught now, fixture stable over 3 runs.

